{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>It shall not give its yield.</b> Even though He said ״וְעָצַר אֶת הַשָּׁמַיִם,״ He returned to say <b>לֹא תִתֵּן</b> etc., to say: even if you sow the earth by channeling rivers and springs, it shall not produce what you bring to it." "<b>And you shall perish quickly.</b> Meaning, even if produce is found for you from earlier years, as they said, of blessed memory (Gittin 56a), they said about him, about Ben Kalba, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:33.586798887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}